    <region left="0" top="22095" width="508" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Note:  The required As should be compared with the peripheral tie reinforcement as<br />calculated from Part 1 clause.3.12.3.5, of the Code. In most instances, no additional<br />steel is specifically needed for diaphragm action at the perimeters.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="22149" width="605" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Separate calculations may need to be carried out for notional load acting in the X-direction . The<br />computation is similar as above. It can easily be shown that the floor diaghragm action is adequately<br />ensured by the 06 steel mesh placed within the concrete topping.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
